---
description: AgentOS architecture and ticket planning — always apply in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

Before planning or implementing work in this repository:

1. Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root.
2. Read `.project/docs/concepts.md` (extension vs service vs packages).
3. Use skills: `agentos-architecture`, `agentos-ticket-planner`, `agentos-bun-runtime`, and `agentos-git-workflow` for commits/PRs (`bun run ci` before every PR to `dev` or `main`; default squash one ticket → `dev`; stack + rebase-merge to batch; `DEPLOYMENT dev->main: …` → `main`; live UI QA when customer-facing).
4. pnpm = install; Bun = run TS/JS; never Node for services.
5. Do not start build tickets 1+ until the user explicitly asks to build.
6. On implement: move the working ticket `todo/` → `in-progress/`. Never move tickets to `done/` (reconciliation owns that).
7. UI base controls must come from `@agentos/ui` (shadcn). Do not use native HTML tags for buttons, inputs, checkboxes, selects, dropdowns, etc. unless specifically required.
8. Source files use **kebab-case** (`shell-root.tsx`, `store.test.ts`). Do not use PascalCase filenames.
9. Package modules use `index.ts` + `lib/` + `tests/` (+ `components/` for React UI).
